  "term": "intergenerational trauma",
  "definition": "Intergenerational trauma is ongoing emotional distress seen in later generations of people who survived large-scale traumatic events, where descendants may experience effects as though they had lived through those events themselves. These trauma-related effects can continue across generations.",
